<https://questions-statements-api.parliament.uk/api/writtenquestions/questions/1891104> <https://forgetmenot.example/accountability#questionText> "To ask His Majesty's Government what assessment they have made of the cost to motor insurance policyholders of compensating victims of collisions involving illegally used e-scooters and e-bikes; and what steps they are taking to address this." <https://forgetmenot.example/accountability#graph/questions-answers> .
<https://questions-statements-api.parliament.uk/api/writtenquestions/questions/1891104> <https://forgetmenot.example/accountability#answerText> "The Secretary of State has made no such assessment. The setting of premiums is a commercial decision for insurers, and the Government does not intervene or seek to control the market." <https://forgetmenot.example/accountability#graph/questions-answers> .
